WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.740
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:02.610
OIKURA'S OBJECTIVE.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:03.740
WHAT IN THE WORLD—

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:04.990
DID SHE WANT TO KNOW?

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.710
Let's go over all the questions that have come up
concerning her mother's disappearance.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.580
In the end, I think that will be
the key to all of this.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.340
In other words,
why was the door to that room locked?

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.220
I have no idea.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.220
Yeah, me neither.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:23.760
You haven't figured it out?

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.850
That's something of a disappointment.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.520
Not to be able to see through
a locked room mystery of this degree.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.310
I've known that you're a fool,
Araragi-senpai,

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:37.110
but to think that even you,
Hanekawa-senpai, are a fool.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.320
No, it's been on my mind.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.160
So, despite knowing it's uncalled for,
I came to see how you were doing.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.080
That perhaps Hanekawa-senpai wasn't able
to be of any help to Araragi-senpai...

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:51.960
And it's just as I thought.

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.880
Maybe you really are past your prime?

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:03.510
And yet, even being at such a degree,
you snatched Araragi-senpai away from me.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.970
That makes me laugh. Dear me.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.930
Despite enticing Araragi-senpai
with those lumps of meat on your chest, right?

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.060
<i>She's totally holding a grudge...</i>

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:18.400
Oh, embarrassing, so embarrassing.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.570
If it was me, I'd be so embarrassed,
I couldn't go on living.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.820
Using my sexual charm
to make Araragi-senpai choose me,

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.780
but only causing him
more trouble in the end.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.700
Come to think of it,
I believe I myself am pathetic.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.660
If I had tagged along,

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.580
Araragi-senpai wouldn't have had
to feel such an emotion.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.630
Because I so easily allowed him
to be taken by Hanekawa-senpai's boobs,

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:41.250
all of this happened.

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:45.760
For making Araragi-senpai go through
such a feeling of helplessness, I'm truly sorry.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:51.890
I really wonder how it would've been
if Araragi-senpai had chosen me back then.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:56.810
But I won't blame you! I won't blame you,
Araragi-senpai. Of course I won't blame you.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:59.020
Everyone makes mistakes after all...

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:00.860
Right, Hanekawa-senpai?

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.490
Hanekawa-senpai,
you'll forgive him as well, right?

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.990
For Araragi-senpai making
the huge mistake of choosing you.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:11.740
If anything, how about
you put it into words and tell him?

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:16.290
Tell him, "My foolishness
isn't your responsibility, Araragi"...

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:18.500
Hey, Ougi...

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.790
As for me...

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.130
As for me, I've already solved it.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.630
That locked room.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:29.140
And where the mother has gone, too.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.390
Well, just a general idea.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.010
In a way.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.310
OWARIMONOGATARI

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:37.020
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST, PART THREE

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:41.650
Well, for me, it was
an extremely simple practice problem.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:45.360
Hanekawa-senpai,
if you absolutely don't understand it,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.660
I'd love to be a good underclassman.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:53.330
If you apologize for having big boobs,
I'll be the bigger person and forgive you.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.120
"I routed all of my nutrition
toward my boobs.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.830
Ougi, younger than me,
my underclassman,

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:04.050
I just can't solve this simple problem,
so please tell me the answer.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.050
I'll never take Araragi
away from you ever again."

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:11.720
If you asked me like that, I might be
compelled to show you the model solution.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:12.600
Ougi!

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.100
I'll be the one to beg you.
That should be fine, right?

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.980
If you already know, please tell me

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:20.350
what happened to Oikura
and her mother three years ago.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:22.770
This troubles me.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:26.440
I'm really angry at Hanekawa-senpai right now.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:29.860
But I can't refuse
if you're the one asking me, Araragi-senpai.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:37.580
So quiet... It's so boring.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:42.380
In the end... Maybe you actually weren't
all that great in your prime, either?

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:43.590
Fine.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.340
Then, Araragi-senpai...

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:49.800
"It was a mistake for me to choose someone
as insignificant as Hanekawa.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.140
Ougi, you're the only partner for me.

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:55.180
I love you, Ougi, more than Hanekawa."

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.640
If you say that, I'll tell you.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.770
The truth about all of this.

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:00.770
Wha—

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:01.900
What's the matter?

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.650
There's no need to hesitate, right?

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:07.570
Because, if you can figure that out,
Oikura-senpai is sure to be...

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.570
...elated by all of this.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:18.160
Now's the time for you
to repay Oikura-senpai for everything, isn't it?

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.160
Or in the end, despite what you may say...

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.790
Do you prioritize Hanekawa-senpai's breasts?

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:28.050
HANEKAWA MAY ACCEPT
HER DEFEAT BY OUGI

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:29.090
AND BE FORCED TO ADMIT IT.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:30.050
I DON'T WANT HANEKAWA
TO ADMIT DEFEAT.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.180
Stop that. Araragi,
don't say anything of that sort.

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:38.350
Even if it's a lie, even if it's for me,

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:41.270
I don't want you to say
anything like that, Araragi.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:42.890
B-But, Hanekawa...

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.560
Of course, I won't say that, either.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.400
No matter how many times it takes,
I'll keep stealing you away, Araragi.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:51.530
Ougi. Give me ten seconds.
I'll prove it...

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:55.030
That Araragi, by choosing me...

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.740
...made the correct choice.

00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:58.080
Ten.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:01.960
Nine.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:05.750
Eight.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:08.630
Seven.

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:11.720
Six.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:15.430
Five.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:19.140
Four.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:22.730
Three.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:24.100
HANEKAWA THINKS.

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:25.310
Two.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.560
HANEKAWA THINKS.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:27.690
One.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:28.860
HANEKAWA THINKS.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:31.480
- Ze—
- You don't have to say zero.

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:34.490
I win.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:35.860
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:38.780
I win.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.490
But this...

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.000
You...

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.040
Was something like this
really your first thought?

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.790
Without careful review?

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:51.880
Just by listening to bits and pieces
of our stories?

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:55.470
And the very first thought you had
was of such a truth?

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:56.680
Yes.

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:58.800
That's how the idea began...

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:02.810
I had a gut feeling and adjusted the reasoning
to fit the situation from there.

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:06.480
What kind of thought process do you have?

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:11.070
That's not sane. To think
that was your first thought...

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:15.240
But in the end, you came
to the same conclusion, didn't you?

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:18.870
Then I don't see
how you can say that to me.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:21.740
Besides, the one furthest from being sane...

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:23.330
...is Oikura-senpai.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:27.920
She is first and foremost
the one acting out of her mind.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:30.920
—WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.340
Araragi... It's no good.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.430
We absolutely cannot tell this to Oikura.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:42.350
Araragi... Earlier, you seemed determined
to tell her the truth, no matter what it was.

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:45.350
But after hearing this,
I think you'll change your mind.

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:46.730
Change my mind?

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:50.360
You shouldn't do that, Hanekawa-senpai.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:52.770
Don't go easy on the fool.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:55.820
You need to make him think for himself,
even for a little bit.

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:58.950
Otherwise, Araragi-senpai
will forever remain the fool.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:06:59.860
NO MATTER HOW MUCH TIME PASSED

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:02.620
You have to make Araragi-senpai
reach this conclusion, too...

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:07.370
To come up with the truth behind it
that makes you nauseous just thinking about it.

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:14.210
The worst truth
I can think of would be...

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:16.720
Hint 1:

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:20.090
Oikura-senpai's mother is already deceased.

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:22.350
She's dead. That means...

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:27.480
Let's see. Oikura's mother
was killed by Oikura's father...

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:31.060
And the strange disappearance
that resembles being spirited away

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:32.860
happened as a result of that...

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:34.440
That's not it at all.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:37.110
You're a kind person, Araragi-senpai.

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:40.490
The worst truth you can possibly imagine
is something that lukewarm?

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:44.370
Then, Hanekawa-senpai,
please give him the second hint.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:45.620
M-Me?

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.870
Hint 2:

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:50.120
Araragi, back when
you were in middle school,

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:54.420
you mistook Oikura's house
to be ruined.

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:58.840
Oikura made a similar mistake
about her mother,

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:00.760
and still does to this day.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:04.890
So her mother was murdered,
Oikura was the murderer,

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:07.890
and she isn't aware of any of it,
or something?

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.390
Hint 3:

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:16.150
Disappearing from a locked room
isn't necessarily escaping from that room.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:20.360
In other words, Oikura unlocked
the door and went in,

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:26.030
but her mother, who was still in the room,
snuck out behind Oikura's back and left the house?

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:29.160
What reason would there be to do that?

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:30.660
Hint 4:

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:36.670
Araragi, if her mother is already deceased,
why can't we find her corpse?

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:38.550
Why is Oikura's mother still treated
as a missing person?

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.420
MISSING PERSON REPORT

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:42.930
Hint 5:

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:45.600
This time, I only
heard everything secondhand...

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:49.970
But Araragi-senpai,
even if you had chosen me as your partner,

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:51.810
based on Oikura-senpai's stories,

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:55.150
I wouldn't have been able to determine
the exact details for "that."

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.270
Now what is...

00:08:57.730 --> 00:08:58.780
..."that"?

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.150
Hint 6:

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:05.910
Oikura's previous house couldn't be cleaned,
as it was filled with garbage.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:07.280
Hint 7:

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.910
Her mother suddenly disappeared one day.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:11.410
Suddenly. One day.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:12.660
Suddenly. On that day.

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:16.040
Then, what about the day before that?

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:17.420
Hint 8:

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:23.170
Because of the family's breakup,
Oikura's mother had a very weak heart.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:27.970
To the point where she cooped herself up
in her room and lost the will to live.

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:29.430
Hint 9:

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:32.890
Oikura-senpai had been
taking care of her mother,

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:37.440
but, over time, the mother
supposedly stopped eating completely.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:39.400
Now, the word "completely" here...

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:40.030
COMPLETELY

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:44.650
Araragi-senpai, you probably thought,
"You say that, but she must've eaten a little, right?"

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:48.160
or some milder interpretation
of your own, didn't you?

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:50.410
Hint 10:

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:52.790
Oikura also said that her mother,

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:57.420
from a certain day, wouldn't reply
even when she talked to her, right?

00:09:57.670 --> 00:09:58.920
Hint 11:

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:01.800
And that she stopped moving
from the corner of her room.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.210
Hint 12:

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:03.380
NOT EATING,

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:04.260
Not eating.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:04.420
NOT LISTENING,

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:05.470
Not listening.

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:06.470
Not speaking.

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:06.680
NOT MOVING.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:07.720
And not moving.

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:10.220
Do you think someone
is even alive at that point?

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:11.510
Hint 13:

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:14.930
Can a middle schooler
really take care of a parent

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:18.400
who's cooped up in their room
for years on end?

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:21.150
I mean, aside from
taking care of a corpse.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:22.530
Hint 14:

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:26.530
How long will a human corpse keep its shape?

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:27.910
Hint 15:

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:29.320
Hint 16:

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:30.700
Hint 17:

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:31.910
Hint 18:

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.040
Hint 19:

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:34.410
Hint 20:

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:35.370
Hint 21:

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:36.210
Hint 22:

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:37.040
Hint 23:

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:37.920
Hint 24:

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:38.710
Hint 25:

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:39.290
Hint 26:

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:40.040
Hint 27:

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:40.670
Hint 28:

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:41.250
Hint 29:

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:50.720
I get it already!

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:59.350
Basically, Oikura, for almost two whole years,
took care of her mother's corpse, right?

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:02.270
Until the corpse fully deteriorated
and disappeared without a trace,

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:03.860
she didn't even notice!

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.110
<i>Yeah... That's right.</i>

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:08.990
<i>In the class assembly two years ago,
I overlooked the truth.</i>

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:09.700
ABOUT OIKURA'S TRAGEDY/INSANITY

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:12.120
<i>I also overlooked it
at the ruined house five years ago.</i>

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:12.780
I

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:16.370
<i>I still can't remember anything about
the childhood friend from six years ago.</i>

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:19.000
<i>Since that's the case,
I can't run from this here.</i>

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:19.830
MUST CONFRONT IT FACE ON.

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:22.090
<i>I can't just avoid things here.</i>

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:24.630
Good answer.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:27.970
It wasn't the fact that
Oikura-senpai's mother suddenly disappeared.

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:31.140
She slowly starved herself to death
by choosing to not eat.

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:34.260
And, after that, she slowly decomposed.

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:37.850
When her original form decomposed
and melted away to where it was unrecognizable,

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:42.860
Oikura-senpai must've had the thought,
"My mother has gone somewhere."

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:45.900
It was just like water evaporating.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:50.200
"I despise water that thinks
it boiled itself on its own," was it?

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:54.490
Yes, but her mother, if I may say so,
boiled herself on her own.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:55.580
Water...

00:11:55.580 --> 00:12:00.710
In other words, Oikura-senpai's mother
essentially evaporated.

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:04.040
Her mother never left the room.

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:08.090
She didn't disappear in a puff of smoke.
She disappeared like water.

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:13.430
But humans don't consist only of water.
What happened to the rest?

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:18.980
It must've been that when they took the garbage
from the house, she was taken along with it.

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:24.810
So... In other words, this means
it was suicide by starvation?

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:26.360
Now, we don't know that.

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:32.070
Even though she lost the will to live,
I think it's different from suicide.

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:38.040
Losing the will to live and wishing to die
are different things to the human heart.

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:40.370
What do you think, Hanekawa-senpai?

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:44.630
I only wish for Oikura
to not find out about this,

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:48.880
and to never find out
for as long as she lives.

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:53.590
But, well, I'm sure she feels
a bit strange about all of this.

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:57.390
Something is off, she feels like
she's avoiding something...

00:12:57.890 --> 00:13:00.890
She has the feeling that
she's pretending not to notice something.

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:04.520
I'm sure she's been feeling that way
for the past three years.

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:07.230
And she will for the rest of her life.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:09.780
No, that ends today.

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:13.280
I'll tell her. I'll be the one to tell her.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:16.410
I'm going back to Oikura's room right now
to tell her everything.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:22.080
It's about time for the guy from town hall
to be leaving her place, right?

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.580
I'll go by myself.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:26.330
It'd be great if you two could wait here.

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:29.300
A-Araragi... Are you serious?

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.720
I'm serious. I said so earlier, right?

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:35.840
That until now, I've always looked at Oikura
and pretended not to see.

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.600
This has gone on for over six years.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:41.180
Just like how she couldn't look
straight at her mother's death,

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:43.440
I couldn't look straight at her.

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:49.110
That's why I can no longer overlook Oikura.

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:52.860
I don't know what will happen
as a result, Araragi-senpai.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:57.200
Oikura-senpai might
hate you more than ever.

00:13:57.530 --> 00:14:00.580
She can't hate me more
than she does now, so it's all right.

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:06.460
Even if she did, if she can love herself
as a result of her hating me,

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:08.960
well, I guess that'd be a bit better.

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:13.720
<i>As her senior on this path,
even though I'm only slightly ahead of her,</i>

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:17.090
<i>I'm going to teach her
how to become happy.</i>

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:22.390
<i>That said, the student is Oikura,
who is the epitome of a distinguished student.</i>

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:26.100
<i>Even concerning happiness,
after learning some tips,</i>

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:28.730
<i>she's sure to pass me in no time.</i>

00:14:29.270 --> 00:14:32.360
<i>But happiness isn't a race.</i>

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:37.950
<i>If she passes me,
I just need to learn from her in return.</i>

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:43.620
<i>That's how we learn, teach,
and take each other to a higher place.</i>

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:46.080
<i>Let's hold a study session.</i>

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:48.500
<i>Even though our foolishness is endless...</i>

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:50.250
<i>We can become wiser together.</i>

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:52.750
<i>We should become happy properly.</i>

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:57.130
Araragi-senpai...

00:14:58.090 --> 00:15:00.390
Are you going to repay
kindness with ingratitude?

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:08.600
<i>Even if it's ingratitude, I'm really glad
I have something I can repay Oikura with.</i>

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:12.570
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:15.690
<i>What you'd call an epilogue...
Or the punchline for this episode.</i>

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:21.280
<i>The next day, my two little sisters, Karen and Tsukihi,
woke me up, and I headed to school.</i>

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:25.250
<i>At that time, I asked my two little sisters
if they remember a child</i>

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:29.960
<i>that was under protective custody
in this house back in grade school.</i>

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.460
<i>Neither of them
remembered such a thing.</i>

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:36.760
<i>In the end, Oikura won't be coming to school...</i>

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:40.090
<i>Even if I went to school today,
I'd never be able to see Oikura.</i>

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:43.430
<i>The promise we made
ended up being discarded,</i>

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:46.600
<i>but that was something
that was completely unavoidable.</i>

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:52.480
The guy from town hall just told me that my aid
will be roughly half of what it is now.

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:55.780
So, apparently, I can't live here anymore.

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:57.490
That said, I'll be all right.

00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:01.320
He said they already found
a slightly smaller municipal condo for me.

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:04.330
So, I'll end up having to move again.

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:07.620
I'll be transferring out
of Naoetsu High School as well.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:11.540
<i>She was surprisingly calm about all of this.</i>

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:17.130
<i>When I see her alone,
when I talk to her alone, Oikura is like this.</i>

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:20.510
<i>Just like the summer break back in 7th grade.</i>

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:27.810
<i>Oikura accepted the theory about her mother
so easily it threw me off.</i>

00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:31.140
I see... That must be how it is.

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:38.400
I knew that I'd have to
leave this town pretty soon...

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:42.610
But you know, that was when I found out
Tetsujo would be taking time off.

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:44.570
So, that's why I went to school.

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:49.410
I felt like something might be there,
that something might change.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.170
And then...

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:57.840
<i>After that, I spoke a bit with Oikura,
then headed back home.</i>

00:16:58.130 --> 00:16:59.670
<i>I didn't end up doing anything else.</i>

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:05.430
<i>And so, I'm not worried about
bumping into Oikura in my classroom today</i>

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:06.930
<i>and am heading to school...</i>

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:08.930
Hi, Araragi-senpai.

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:13.230
Don't you "Hi" me...

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:16.690
Hey, Ougi, why did you
head home yesterday?

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:18.070
I told you to wait for me.

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:20.940
Hanekawa-senpai said
we should go home.

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:23.780
Why would Hanekawa say that?

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:25.870
She was saying it in a positive way.

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:28.870
Kind of like,
"Let's leave them alone."

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:31.290
No, don't say it was "in a positive way."

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:35.920
How surprised do you think I was
when I saw you guys weren't in that courtyard?

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:38.670
About yesterday...
That was a loss for me.

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:42.670
I'm terribly sorry.
I had underestimated you, to be honest.

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:47.180
I was completely under the impression
that you'd turn tail and run...

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:50.770
At the very end, you showed me
some unexpected gusto.

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:54.020
Somehow, it all feels a bit strange.

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:57.480
As soon as you transfer to this school,
Tetsujo went on maternity leave...

00:17:57.900 --> 00:17:59.360
Oikura comes to school...

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:01.990
And as I was processing that,
she transfers away.

00:18:02.150 --> 00:18:05.490
Things that were at a standstill,
things that were avoided,

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:09.280
as if they were suddenly remembered,
felt as though they suddenly started moving along.

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:13.710
Oh, so Oikura-senpai is transferring
to another school?

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:15.420
I didn't know that.

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:18.000
She was well cast, too.

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:22.090
But really, I hope she can do well
wherever she transfers to.

00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:25.930
I'm sure she'll succeed if she's in
a new place where nobody knows her.

00:18:26.510 --> 00:18:28.300
Because of Araragi-senpai.

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:29.800
Thanks to you.

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:37.060
Ougi, what are you doing in a place like this?

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:40.320
Is your home nearby?

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:43.190
I've been looking for a lost child.

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:45.700
That was my original starting point.

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:49.240
I'll chalk this one up as my loss...

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:52.990
But, at the least,
if I was allowed to be a sore loser...

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:55.870
The first move was just something
to watch how things unfolded.

00:18:56.210 --> 00:19:02.920
The objective of seeing how you behave
with your childhood friends has been met.

00:19:02.920 --> 00:19:06.010
So, as far as balance goes,
I think it was perfect for me to lose here.

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:08.970
Please be careful, Araragi-senpai.

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:12.310
It might not go this well next time.

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.350
No one knows what the future holds,

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:16.600
because it's as dark
as the streets at night.

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:20.940
I see... That's a shame.

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:24.110
I thought I'd be able
to get along with Oikura.

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:30.530
But I guess we should celebrate
Oikura's new start in life for now.

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:33.910
That's true.
Ougi said something like that as well.

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:39.120
Araragi, I have to go request
a leave of absence,

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:41.500
so can you head
to the classroom without me?

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:42.880
Oh, sure...

00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:44.960
Wait, request for a leave of absence?

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:47.840
What? You're going to
quit Naoetsu High as well?

00:19:47.840 --> 00:19:50.430
No, time off. A leave of absence.

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:55.430
You know how I'm planning to take a trip
and wander around after we graduate, right?

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:58.480
I thought I'd go scout locations first,

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:00.560
so I'm going to take a quick trip
around the world.

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:04.070
I'll be gone about a month,
so I'll leave things to you.

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:08.820
If I see Oshino somewhere during this trip,
I'll reach out to him for you.

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:12.780
Then, if you see Oshino somewhere,
tell him I've met his niece.

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:17.660
Yeah. Well, I'll be sure to tell him that.

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:26.670
NO SUBJECT / *MARK AS UNREAD
TO KOYOKOYO,
I REALLY HAD BROKEN A BONE ON MY FINGER
SO I'LL HEAD TO SCHOOL TODAY
AFTER GOING TO THE HOSPITAL.

00:20:27.010 --> 00:20:29.050
Why does this look like an old telegraph?

00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:31.300
TO YOKOYOKO

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:32.680
Side-side (yoko-yoko)?

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:37.680
TO YOKOYOKO
OIKURA CAME TO APOLOGIZE THIS MORNING.
I FORGAVE HER. I'M ALL RIGHT NOW
(THOUGH I HAVE A BROKEN BONE)

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:44.520
<i>Apparently Oikura had kept her promise
to make up with Senjyogahara.</i>

00:20:44.900 --> 00:20:45.690
<i>I'm glad.</i>

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:49.940
<i>I should show Hanekawa this text
before she leaves for her trip.</i>

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:55.950
KOYOKOYO, I'M SORRY TO MAKE YOU WORRY SO MUCH.
I'LL GIVE YOU LOTS OF FRENCH KISSES
ON OUR NEXT DATE, SO FORGIVE ME
I'M ADDICTED TO YOUR FRENCH KISSES

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:58.580
These texts are turning into something
I can't show anyone!

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:02.080
A MESSAGE FROM OIKURA.
SHE SAID "UNDER THE DESK."
FROM YOUR LEFT

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:03.830
FROM YOUR LEFT

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:07.840
<i>"From your left"?
What kind of a greeting is that?</i>

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:14.090
<i>Back in the day,
during summer break five years ago.</i>

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:19.430
<i>Hadn't I had found a similar envelope
underneath a tea table in a ruined house?</i>

00:21:20.060 --> 00:21:23.350
<i>However, that envelope was empty.</i>

00:21:23.480 --> 00:21:27.480
<i>From how it felt, I could tell
that this time around, there was paper inside.</i>

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:32.860
<i>The envelope didn't have a sender or a recipient
on either the front or the back.</i>

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:37.740
<i>However, it was obvious
who had taped this to my desk.</i>

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:42.750
<i>Sodachi Oikura.
She'd kept all of her promises.</i>

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:46.500
<i>Suddenly disappearing without warning...</i>

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:50.960
<i>Oikura, for now, has become a girl
who wouldn't do that.</i>

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:55.260
<i>It was a small change,
but it was still a change for her.</i>

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:57.640
<i>That made me happy,</i>

00:21:57.640 --> 00:22:00.810
<i>but I felt like she'd gone ahead of me,
which left me feeling a bit lonely.</i>

00:22:01.640 --> 00:22:04.640
<i>Here, I felt I should show
that I've grown up as well,</i>

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:07.650
<i>so I didn't rip and tear into it
like I did five years ago.</i>

00:22:08.190 --> 00:22:10.480
<i>I opened the envelope
as carefully as possible</i>

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:13.280
<i>and pulled out multiple sheets
of paper from within.</i>

00:22:14.530 --> 00:22:18.530
<i>Now, are the contents of the letter
a mathematics quiz?</i>

00:22:18.530 --> 00:22:21.240
<i>A letter of thanks she's unlikely to write?</i>

00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:23.620
<i>Or will it be a message insulting me?</i>

00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:25.790
<i>It's possible it'll be all of the above...</i>

00:22:26.710 --> 00:22:27.580
<i>Now, let's see.</i>

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:34.420
<i>I couldn't help but smile.</i>

00:22:35.380 --> 00:24:20.187
<i>Hey, what do you think was written?</i>
